The attached image displays the physical characterization of Nano-11 nanoparticles. The left panel, a Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image, shows the spherical or cauliflower-like morphology of the Nano-11 particles, which appear as individual entities or small aggregates. A 50 nm scale bar is provided for reference. The right panel, a histogram of particle diameter determined by dynamic light scattering, indicates that Nano-11 particles have a relatively uniform size distribution, predominantly ranging from 30 to 110 nm, with a peak around 70-80 nm. This characterization is crucial for understanding their efficient uptake by dendritic cells and their function as vaccine adjuvants.